 r←Test_Log_103(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;tempDir;msg;rc;filename;list;expected
⍝ The usage data files offered for download are listed newest first, whatever order the file
⍝ system delivers them in, and nothing but usage data files is listed: neither the application
⍝ log nor its year-end backups, nor usage data files of another type.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 r←T._Failed

 tempDir←∆GetTempDir'-Log/'
 rc←'Create!'F.CheckPath tempDir
 Assert rc
 :For filename :In 'usage-data-2024.zip' 'usage-data-2026-08.zip' 'usage-data-2022.zip' 'usage-data-2025.zip' 'usage-data-2025-11.zip' 'usage-data-2026-08.csv' 'app-log-2025.bkp.zip' 'app-log.txt'
     (⊂'Group,Name,Version,Year,Month,Downloads')F.NPUT(tempDir,filename)1
 :EndFor
 list←'zip'##.Server.ListUsageDataFiles tempDir
 expected←'usage-data-2026-08.zip' 'usage-data-2025.zip' 'usage-data-2025-11.zip' 'usage-data-2024.zip' 'usage-data-2022.zip'
 →T.GoToTidyUp expected≢list

 r←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 (rc msg)←F.RmDirByForce tempDir
 msg Assert rc=0
⍝Done
